2. High‑level module map for Emphemsa

Core modules:

OntologyKernelEmphemsaRole: Load Emphemsa‑style blueprints (organisms, fields, regimes).

StateLatticeRole: Hold the live simulation state as a lattice/grid of fields.

FieldDynamicsEngineRole: Evolve fields over time (warp, gravity, stress, charge, etc.).

RegimeOrchestratorRole: Switch modes (stable, critical, exotic, failure).

Constraint & Permission LayerRole: Enforce envelopes, limits, and allowed behaviors.

Telemetry & Trace LayerRole: Output time‑series, snapshots, and regime maps.

3. Emphemsa DSL seed organism

You can treat Emphemsa as a slightly more abstract, field‑centric cousin of Septseptseptium:

organism EmphemsaCore as field_organism {
  identity {
    designer        "C. Matthew Blackwell"
    engine_family   "Emphemsa"
    role            "core-field-organism"
  }

  fields {
    warp_field      type: "metric_distortion"
    grav_field      type: "gradient_control"
    stress_field    type: "structural_load"
    charge_field    type: "energy_potential"
  }

  regimes {
    stable      when stress_field < 0.4 and warp_field < 0.6
    critical    when stress_field in [0.4, 0.8]
    exotic      when warp_field >= 0.8
    failure     when stress_field > 0.9 or grav_field > 0.95
  }

  permissions {
    allow_warp      when regime in [stable, exotic]
    clamp_output    when regime == critical
    shutdown        when regime == failure
  }
}

